  "In Part 5, we synthesize our WACC, capital structure weighting, and divisional risk analytics into an Enterprise Corporate Hurdle Rate & Capital Allocation Control Suite. In corporate treasury and boardroom planning, senior finance executives establish an enterprise Capital Allocation Matrix that aligns divisional project proposals with appropriate hurdle rates. The corporate hurdle rate control tower coordinates three primary analytical layers:\n1. Enterprise Benchmark Hurdle Rate: Master corporate WACC calculated with market value weights, providing the baseline for corporate-level investments. 2. Divisional Beta & Risk Adjustments: Tailored hurdle rates assigned to individual business units (e.g., Core Utilities vs Growth Tech vs High-Risk M&A). 3. Capital Investment Approval Routing: Automated comparison of internal proposal returns against tailored hurdle rates, certifying value-accretive capital allocation. (Step 2: Record secondary interest & fee accrual adjustment ($15,800).)",
