          explanation: "DFL = EBIT / (EBIT - Interest) = $600,000 / ($600,000 - $200,000) = $600,000 / $400,000 = 1.50x. Therefore, % Delta EPS = DFL * % Delta EBIT = 1.50x * 10% = 15.0% expansion in EPS."
