          explanation: "Using the CIRP equation: F0 = S0 * [(1 + r_home) / (1 + r_foreign)] = $1.2000 * (1.05 / 1.02) = $1.2000 * 1.02941 = $1.2353 per EUR. The Euro trades at a forward premium because US interest rates exceed Eurozone rates."
