        "The primary metric tracked by financial sponsors, rating agencies, and investment committees is Total Debt-to-EBITDA Leverage. In our enterprise buyout, the company initiates operations at a total leverage multiple of six point zero times EBITDA (one billion five hundred million dollars in debt on two hundred fifty million dollars in EBITDA), with Senior Secured Leverage standing at three point two times EBITDA ($800M Term Loan B).",
        "As our five-year operational forecast unfolds, EBITDA expands at a steady compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of six point zero percent, growing from two hundred fifty million dollars in Year 1 to three hundred fifteen point two million dollars ($315.2M) in Year 5, driven by operational efficiencies, pricing optimization, and working capital rationalization.",
