        "In the United States, foreign sovereign investments are governed by the Committee on Foreign Investment in the United States (CFIUS), an interagency committee authorized under Section 721 of the Defense Production Act. The enactment of the Foreign Investment Risk Review Modernization Act (FIRRMA) of 2018 vastly expanded CFIUS jurisdiction. Previously focused primarily on transactions where a foreign entity acquired majority control of a U.S. business, FIRRMA authorized CFIUS to review non-passive, non-controlling investments in U.S. businesses involving critical technology, critical infrastructure, or sensitive personal data (TID U.S. businesses).",
